# Who reviews what.
#
# Every path has a default owner, so nothing lands without an owner attached.
#
# HONEST LIMITATION, 26 August 2026: there is exactly one owner, and he is also
# the only author. GitHub does not let an author approve their own pull request,
# so branch protection requires a pull request and a green deterministic CI run
# but does NOT require an approving review — a requirement that cannot be
# satisfied is not a control, it is a bypass everyone learns to perform.
#
# WHEN A SECOND REVIEWER EXISTS, do two things together:
#   1. add them below, and
#   2. raise required_approving_review_count to 1 in branch protection.
# Neither is worth much without the other. Readiness plan Task 9 and Task 11 own
# this; open question 2 asks who fills the reviewer role.
#
# A GitHub team handle (@millcreek/gis) is preferable to individual accounts once
# an organization exists, because it survives staff changes and an individual
# handle does not.

* @buschbrian

